EFFORT vs RESULT"] you only need ONE mental model. Just one.&nbsp; Effort versus Result. In the market:&nbsp; Effort is volume — how much energy,&nbsp; how much money is being used.&nbsp; Result is the candle — how&nbsp; far price actually moved.&nbsp; Think of it like pushing a car up a hill. Your foot on the gas pedal is the effort.&nbsp; How far the car moves is the result. Case number one: You press the gas.&nbsp; The car moves easily. Big effort.&nbsp; Big result. Everything matches.&nbsp; On the chart, that's a big candle&nbsp; with high volume underneath.&nbsp; Lots of buyers. Lots of conviction.&nbsp; The move is real. Like a whole stadium standing up to cheer.&nbsp; That's genuine excitement. Case number two: You slam the gas pedal.&nbsp; The engine roars. Fuel is burning.&nbsp; But the car barely moves. There's something blocking the road.&nbsp; On the chart, that's a tiny candle&nbsp; with MASSIVE volume underneath.&nbsp; This is called Absorption. What's happening?&nbsp; Buyers are pushing hard, but&nbsp; there's an invisible wall.&nbsp;

