Smart Money Exit"] That might be exactly when smart&nbsp; money is walking out the door.&nbsp; Pattern three: No Supply Test. After an uptrend, price pulls back a little.&nbsp; You're worried. "Is this a correction?"&nbsp; Then you look at volume: a small&nbsp; red candle, and volume is VERY low.&nbsp; The market is asking a question:&nbsp; "Does anyone want to sell here?"&nbsp; And low volume answers: "No. Not really." That's a No Supply test.&nbsp; Sellers are absent. The uptrend is likely to continue.&nbsp; Like testing if the fire is hot. You put your hand near it — it's cool.&nbsp; Safe to move forward. Three patterns.&nbsp; One mental model. Effort versus Result.&nbsp; That's enough to read eighty percent of&nbsp; what volume is telling you on any chart.&nbsp;
